---
id: SCR-003   kind: screen   name: Weekly Timetable
app: APP-001   module: MOD-002   screen_type: calendar   surface: phone
roles: [ROL-002]
tiers: {purpose: default, regions: default, actions: default, states: default}
provenance: ["compass:SCR-003", "model:spec.scrn", "user:FTR-001", "user:FTR-002"]
stories: [US-S001, US-S002]
---
purpose: Members browse the weekly class schedule and choose a class to view or book.
route: {name: weekly_timetable, path: /weekly_timetable, params: [], guard: [signed_in, role_has_access]}
reached_from: [SCR-001.submit_credentials, SCR-002.submit_code]   leads_to: [SCR-001, SCR-004, SCR-006, SCR-007, SCR-010, SCR-S001, SCR-S002, SCR-S004]
regions:   # alphabetical by key; the order carries no meaning
  - {key: day_items, shape: collection, what: the classes on the chosen day, bind: [ENT-001.title, ENT-001.starts_at, ENT-001.ends_at, ENT-001.instructor_name], importance: supporting, cardinality: few}
  - {key: schedule, shape: schedule, what: the classes over time, bind: [ENT-001.starts_at, ENT-001.ends_at], importance: primary}
actions:
  - {key: open_class_details, importance: secondary, intent: navigate, what: go to Class Details, effect: [go SCR-004]}
states:   # what each must communicate, not how
  - {kind: "domain:no_availability", message: Nothing can be chosen in this range; say why and suggest another range.}
  - {kind: empty, message: Nothing is scheduled in the range; say so and how to add something.}
  - {kind: error, message: Something failed; say what happened in plain words and offer a retry.}
  - {kind: forbidden, message: The user's role may not see or do this; say so and where to go instead.}
  - {kind: loading, message: Nothing to show yet; the user must still see that content is coming.}
  - {kind: offline, message: "There is no network; show saved data, and say which actions are unavailable and why."}
  - {kind: stale, message: The data shown may be out of date; the user can ask for the latest.}
copy_keys: [lib.calendar.domain.no_availability, lib.calendar.empty, lib.common.error, lib.common.forbidden, lib.common.loading, lib.common.offline, lib.common.stale, scr_003.day_items_label, scr_003.open_class_details, scr_003.schedule_label, scr_003.title]
accessibility: every region and action has a text label that assistive technology can read
acceptance:
  - GIVEN the user has typical data and a working network WHEN the user uses Weekly Timetable for its main purpose THEN the main purpose is achieved and the result is confirmed in plain words
  - GIVEN the user has no data for Weekly Timetable yet WHEN Weekly Timetable loads THEN the empty state says why there is nothing and what the user can do next
  - GIVEN the server fails when Weekly Timetable asks for data or sends a change WHEN the failure is received THEN the user is told in plain words that something went wrong, nothing is lost, and a retry is offered
mock: {profiles: [empty, typical], hero: ["ENT-001:cancelled", "ENT-001:scheduled"]}

---
id: SCR-008   kind: screen   name: Pay for Pack
app: APP-001   module: MOD-003   screen_type: checkout   surface: phone
roles: [ROL-002]
tiers: {purpose: default, regions: default, actions: default, states: default}
provenance: ["compass:SCR-008", "model:spec.scrn", "user:FTR-003"]
stories: [US-S003]
---
purpose: Members pay the studio directly for their selected pack using UPI or card.
route: {name: pay_for_pack, path: /pay_for_pack, params: [], guard: [signed_in, role_has_access]}
reached_from: [SCR-007.open_pay_for_pack]   leads_to: [SCR-009]
regions:   # alphabetical by key; the order carries no meaning
  - {key: amount_due_class_pack, shape: key_values, what: what the user pays for and the amount due, bind: [ENT-003.price], importance: primary}
  - {key: amount_due_payment, shape: key_values, what: what the user pays for and the amount due, bind: [ENT-004.amount], importance: primary}
  - {key: methods_payment, shape: options, what: the ways the user can pay, bind: [OP-S013], importance: primary, cardinality: few, freshness: on_open}
actions:
  - {key: pay, importance: primary, intent: pay, what: pay the amount due, precondition: a way to pay is chosen and an amount is due, effect: [call OP-S015, external_flow payments, go SCR-009], errors: [network, forbidden, validation_failed, conflict], flags: [idempotent]}
states:   # what each must communicate, not how
  - {kind: "domain:conflict", message: "Something in the order changed, such as a price or availability; the user must agree to the change before paying."}
  - {kind: "domain:payment_declined", message: The payment was declined; no order is placed and another method can be tried.}
  - {kind: "domain:payment_pending", message: The payment result is not known yet; the user cannot pay again meanwhile.}
  - {kind: error, message: Something failed; say what happened in plain words and offer a retry.}
  - {kind: forbidden, message: The user's role may not see or do this; say so and where to go instead.}
  - {kind: loading, message: Nothing to show yet; the user must still see that content is coming.}
  - {kind: offline, message: "There is no network; show saved data, and say which actions are unavailable and why."}
  - {kind: success, message: What the user did worked; say what changed.}
copy_keys: [lib.checkout.domain.conflict, lib.checkout.domain.payment_declined, lib.checkout.domain.payment_pending, lib.common.error, lib.common.forbidden, lib.common.loading, lib.common.offline, lib.common.success, scr_008.amount_due_class_pack_label, scr_008.amount_due_payment_label, scr_008.methods_payment_label, scr_008.pay, scr_008.title]
analytics: [payment_paid]
accessibility: the result of pay the amount due is announced to assistive technology
acceptance:
  - GIVEN the user has typical data and a working network WHEN the user uses Pay for Pack for its main purpose THEN the main purpose is achieved and the result is confirmed in plain words
  - GIVEN the user pays and the payment is declined WHEN the decline is received THEN the user is told the order was not paid for and why if known, no order is placed, and another payment method can be tried
  - GIVEN the result of what the user did is not known yet WHEN the user is on Pay for Pack THEN the user is told the result is pending and cannot repeat the action by mistake, and the final result appears here when known
  - GIVEN a signed-in members on Pay for Pack WHEN they pay the amount due THEN the change is saved and the person reaches SCR-009
mock: {profiles: [broken, typical], hero: ["ENT-004:paid", "ENT-004:pending"]}

